      field: WholeDeclaration
    }
  ],

  reason: "WHY RUST IS STILL NEEDED HERE: the subject is the HOST PROCESS -- stdout bytes and an exit status -- and it is reached from a returned interpreter Value. Neither end has a .dag denotation today: there is no modeled carrier for a running process's standard output, and no modeled projection of the interpreter's own Value representation, so the fold between them cannot be written in the substrate it is bridging into. This is a boundary item, not seed-shrink debt.\n\nWHAT IT REMOVED: gunbc.cli_dispatch_surface's scm row carried CliRefusesUnwired -- the compiler's own dispatch model recording that the scm command family computed answers no user could invoke. Every modeled scm entry was therefore specification without execution. With this route bound, the scm log and status answers reach an operator, which is the only reason the .dag side of this change is worth anything. scm_init is deliberately NOT in this change: observing an absence and then writing unconditionally can still truncate the bytes it claims to refuse, and the atomic create-only write that closes that does not exist yet, so init lands with the primitive rather than being claimed reachable here.\n\nHAND-ITEM DELTA: +26 FROM THE MERGE BASE, ENUMERATED ABOVE.\n\nTHE COUNT IS STATED AS A DERIVATION RATHER THAN A NUMBER, because typing the number is how this row was wrong twice. It said +11 while the classifier test module added thirteen items nobody had listed, and then +25 while a test added after the row was written -- a_printable_response_whose_exit_is_not_a_process_exit_is_malformed_and_prints_nothing, the one that closed review 58518 -- sat outside it. Both times the receipt was edited as a step SEPARATE from the code it admits, so anything added afterwards fell silently outside the subject. Re-derive instead of trusting: for each of the two test modules, the entries are the module itself, every `fn` in it that carries #[test], and every `fn` in it that does not. 5 production + (cli_wire_outcome_tests: 1 module + 0 helpers + 5 tests) + (cli_wire_classify_tests: 1 module + 5 helpers + 9 tests) = 26.\n\nCHILD ITEMS CARRY THEIR NESTED MODULE PATH -- v1_compiler.cli_run.cli_wire_classify_tests, not v1_compiler.cli_run -- because that is where the declaration actually lives, and a roster whose identities do not resolve to the code cannot be checked against it. The outcome module's five were flattened onto the parent path when first written; they are corrected here rather than left as a second convention beside the new one.\n\nReproducible from the merge base, never the moving tip: git diff $(git merge-base origin/main HEAD)...HEAD -- src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs src/v1/stage0/src/main.rs. Two further .rs files differ and are GENERATED projections rather than hand-authored items -- gunbc_cli_dispatch_surface.rs and gunbc_rust_source_type_bindings.rs, both regenerated from their .dag authority -- so they are outside this roster's subject by construction, not by exemption. One of the 26, exit_status_for_class, is a RELOCATION rather than new behaviour: its body was moved out of main.rs's exit_status_for, which now delegates to it, so the process-exit path gained no behaviour and was only made callable from the wire path beside it. It is counted because the roster counts hand-authored DECLARATIONS, and netting a relocation against an addition is the arithmetic gunbc.seed_growth_admission refuses.\n\nWHY THE CLASSIFIER AND THE OUTCOME ARE TWO ITEMS: the classification is a question about a value and the outcome is a decision about a process, and fusing them would have put the write-or-refuse decision inside a match arm in main.rs where no test could reach it. Splitting them is what made the five-case matrix authorable, including the two cases that carry the actual safety content -- an unprintable response REFUSES rather than printing nothing, and an exit_failure carrying status zero is refused on the wire path exactly as it already was on the process-exit path.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Delete CliWireClass, classify_cli_wire and their tests when the interpreter publishes a modeled projection of a returned Value against a declared type -- an inhabitance decision the substrate answers, rather than a hand-written field-by-field match on the host Value representation. Delete CliWireOutcome, cli_wire_outcome, exit_status_for_class and their tests when std models a process's standard output and exit status as a carrier the .dag side can produce directly, so a command entry returns the whole host effect and the seed only executes it. Both triggers name a CAPABILITY the substrate does not have today; neither is discharged by any artifact short of it, and in particular neither is discharged by moving this Rust to another file.",
  current_boundary: "gunbc.cli_wire_host_admission -> v1_compiler.cli_run cli_wire_outcome -> v1_compiler.main run_verb -> the host process stdout and exit status"
}
